a:15:{s:6:"item-0";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:85:"Day - 1: Arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA) Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)";s:11:"description";s:204:"We will meet you outside of Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA), waiting with a warm greeting and take you towards your hotel. In the evening, our team will explain overall pre - tour plan in brief.

";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-1";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:58:"Day - 2: Drive to Pokhara (820m / 2690 ft) 6-7 hours drive";s:11:"description";s:476:"Our remarkable journey begins with bus ride from Kathmandu to Pokhara passing through the mesmerizing scenery of beautiful landscape. For much of the journey, the road runs parallel to the Trishuli and later Marsyangdi river, offering scenic views of terraced farmlands, valleys, and rolling green hills. Finally the busy capital city connects to the peaceful lake city of Pokhara. After refreshment at the hotel, we will take you around the beautiful tourist hub of lakeside.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-2";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:107:" Day – 3: Drive from Pokhara to Ulleri and trek to Banthanti (2210m / 7250 ft) 3 hrs drive and 2 hrs trek";s:11:"description";s:658:"The journey from Pokhara to Ulleri begins with a scenic drive along winding mountain roads, passing through terraced fields, rivers, and charming hillside villages. The road gradually climbs higher, offering glimpses of Annapurna peaks before reaching the Gurung village of Ulleri. From here, the trek towards Banthanti initiates with stone-paved steps and lush forests. The trail is surrounded by rhododendron and oak trees along with fresh mountain air. As you walk deeper into the forest leaving the roads behind, and after a few hours of steady trekking, you arrive at Banthanti, which is perfect for rest and Himalayan views. Overnight at tea house.

";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-3";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:74:"Day – 4: Trek from Banthanti to Ghorepani (2780m / 9121 ft) 3-4 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:505:"The trek from Banthanti to Ghorepani is a refreshing walk through enchanting section of Annapurna region. The trail winds gently uphill, shaded by dense rhododendron and oak trees. The path allows you to soak in the natural beauty and serenity of the forest. After few hours of trekking, the traditional houses of Ghorepani  covered with Magar community can be seen. From the cozy tea houses of Ghorepani, we can see stunning views of Mt. Annapurna, Mt. Dhaulagiri and Mt. Nilgiri. Overnight at tea house.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-4";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:78:"Day – 5: Trek form Ghorepani/Poon Hill to Tadapani (2680m/8727ft) 5 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:596:"Early in the morning, we hike up to Poon Hill (3210m) observing the breathtaking sunrise over the Mt. Annapurna and Mt. Dhaulagiri ranges, where golden rays light up the snowcapped peaks in an unforgettable panorama. After returning to hotel for breakfast, we continue our hike towards another beautiful hilltop Tadapani through enchanting forests having fresh mountain air. Then the path leads to a peaceful, small village Tadapani, surrounded by forest. From here, we can enjoy the closer, dramatic views of the Himalayas such as Annapurna South, himchuli, and Mt. Fishtail in a serene setting.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-5";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:69:"Day –   6: Trek from Tadapani to Chomrong (2060m/6759ft) 5 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:668:"The trek from Tadapani to Chomrong is a beautiful journey that takes you deeper into the heart of the Annapurna region. Leaving Tadapani, the trail descends through lush rhododendron and pine trees with the sound of streams accompanying the walk. The path winds down to the charming Gurung village of Chuile and continues through terraced farmlands and small settlements. After crossing a suspension bridge over the Kimrong Khola, the trail climbs uphill, eventually leading to Chomrong, a welcoming village perched on the hillside. The views of Annapurna south and fishtail feel close and majestic, making Chomrong a perfect gateway to the higher Annapurna sanctuary.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-6";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:66:"Day – 7: Trek from Chomrong to Dovan (2600m/8580ft) 5-6 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:829:"Our hike from Chomrong to Dovan takes you closer to the Annapurna sanctuary, with mix of steep descents and ascents through charming villages and lush forests. The trails first, drops down a long stone staircase to suspension bridge crossing the river. After the crossing, a steady climb begins through terraced fields and forest reaching the small settlement of Sinuwa. From here, the landscape become quieter and more secluded as the trails enters dense bamboo and rhododendron forest passing through Bamboo    village and enjoying the cool shade of forest. The walk is peaceful with the sound of rushing rivers and glimpses of towering cliffs. Finally, we reach Dovan, a tranquil stop surrounded by forested hills, offering a restful atmosphere before climb towards Deurali and the Annapurna base camp. Overnight at tea house.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-7";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:64:"Day – 8: Trek from Dovan to Deurali (3200m/10545ft) 4 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:735:"Leaving the quite forested village Dovan, the trail follows Modhi khola valley with the sound of river enhoing below. The path winds through dense forests of bamboo and rhododendron, often shaded and cool, with occasional clearings that reveal dramatic cliffs and waterfalls cascading down the hillside. Passing through the small settlement of Himalaya the climb continue  gradually and the air feels fresher as you gain altitude. The vegetation begins to thin, giving way to more open landscapes with sweeping views. Finally, after several hours of hiking you reach Deurali, a serene stop nestled at foot of towering peaks, offering breathtaking views and a sense of being close to the heart of the Himalayas. Overnight at tea house. ";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-8";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:81:"Day – 9: Trek from Deurali to Annapurna Base Camp (4130m/13590ft) 4-5 hrs hike ";s:11:"description";s:918:" The most awaiting day Finally today, the hike from Deurali to Annapurna Base Camp (ABC) is one of the most dramatic and rewarding section of the journey. The trail gradually ascends along the Modhi khola, with the landscape opening wider as dense forests give way to alpine meadows and rugged cliffs. Soon you reach Machhapuchhre Base Camp(3700m), a stunning viewpoint surrounded by snowcapped peaks, where Machhapuchhre (fishtail) rises sharply above. From MBC, the trail continues gently uphill across a high alpine plateau and with each step the panorama expands. Finally, after a few hours of steady hikes, you arrive at Annapurna Base Camp (4130M) a breathtaking amphitheater of mountains known as the Annapurna Sanctuary. Here, the peaks stand so closer and towering that you feel completely immersed in the heart of the Himalaya, making it the highlight and ultimate reward of the trek. Overnight at tea house.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-9";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:72:"  Day - 10:  Annapurna Base Camp to Bamboo ( 2310m/ 7580ft) 5-6 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:809:"The hike from Annapurna Base Camp to Bamboo marks the beginning of the return journey offering a different perspective of the mountain you just conquered. Leaving   the high alpine plateau of ABC, the trail gradually descends through the same valley we hiked up. Passing Machhapuchhre Base Camp once again, the path winds through open meadows, rocky ridges, and patches of rhododendron forest, with the snowcap peaks slowly fading into the distance. As you descend further, the air grow warmer and the vegetation denser, returning to bamboo groves and pine forests. The trails passess small settlements and teahouses, where trekkers can rest and enjoy the serene surroundings.  After several hours descent you arrive at Bamboo, a peaceful village. Overnight couple of hours of descent you arrive at teahouse. ";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-10";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:61:"Day – 11: Bamboo to Jhinu Danda (1780m/5800ft) 5-6 hrs hike";s:11:"description";s:571:" The hike back from Bamboo to Jhinu Danda is a beautiful and refreshing descent. Leaving bamboo, the trail gently up and downhill through dense rhododendron, oak and bamboo forests, with the sound of birds and nearby streams accompanying your walk. Along the way, we pass traditional Gurung settlement offering glimpses of local life in the mountains. The path eventually leads to Jhinu Danda, a charming village known for its neutral hot springs. Here, trekkers can relax and soak in the warm waters, soothing tired muscles after days of trekking, overnight at teahouse.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-11";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:51:"Day – 12: Jhinu to Pokhara (820m / 2690 ft) 3 hrs";s:11:"description";s:479:"After a refreshing morning in Jhinu Danda, where many trekkers enjoy a relaxing dip in the natural hot springs by the Modi Khola, the journey back toward civilization begins. A short walk down to the jeep station connects you to the road.  The drive gradually transitions from mountain tracks to smoother highways as you approach Pokhara within couple of hours, we arrive in the beautiful lakeside city. After the arrival, in the afternoon we explore Pokhara. Overnight at hotel.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-12";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:50:"Day – 13: Pokhara to Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)";s:11:"description";s:159:"After completing the incredible days in Himalaya, today marks the return to Kathmandu. In the morning, we take a scenic drive form Pokhara back to the capital.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-13";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:41:"Day – 14: Kathmandu city tour/free time";s:11:"description";s:308:" Today we explore the Kathmandu, a living museum home to seven World Heritage Sites that showcase Nepal’s rich history, culture, and spirituality. A day tour of these sites offers an unforgettable journey through ancient temples, royal palaces, and sacred monuments that reflect art and tradition of Nepal.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-14";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:21:"Day – 15: Departure";s:11:"description";s:139:" After breakfast, as your time, our representative from Nepal Dream Adventure  will drop you off at the Airport before your flight departs.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}}

a:12:{s:6:"item-0";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:42:"Day 1: Arrived in Kathmandu(1350m/4429ft0)";s:11:"description";s:196:"We meet you outside of Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA). We will be waiting with a warm greeting & take you to your hotel. An evening will have a tour briefing about hole trip. over in hotel.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-1";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:54:"Day 2: Kathmandu drive to syabrubesi (1550m/5085ft/6h)";s:11:"description";s:192:"Today you will start trek with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to syabrubesi the gateway to Langtang and enjoy the Picturesque landscapes along the way and get ready for the adventure ahead.

";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-2";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:48:"Day 3: Syabrubesi to Lama hotel(2380m/7880ft/6h)";s:11:"description";s:136:"After breakfast you will start trek from Syabrubesi to lama hotel, immersing yourself in the peaceful atmosphere of the Langtang region.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-3";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:47:"Day 4: Lama hotel to Langtang(3430m/11253ft/7h)";s:11:"description";s:217:"We continue walking from lama hotel to Langtang where you will be surrounded by stunning mountain vista and luse green forest you will explore the charming Langtang village and Soka in the nature beauty of the reason.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-4";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:51:"Day 5: Langtang to Kyanjin Gompa (3870m/12697ft/4h)";s:11:"description";s:203:"We continue trek from Langtang to Kyanjing Gompa a renowned monastery in the area, enjoy the breathtaking views of the snowcapped peaks and immerses yourself in the spiritual atmosphere of the monastery.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-5";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:44:"Day 6: Acclimatization day at Kyanjin Gompa ";s:11:"description";s:231:"We take one more day at kyanjin Gompa to explore the beauty of Langtang and acclimatize ourselves to the increasing altitude before heading for the Yala peak. the highlight to visit today Kyanjin ri, cheese factory and monastery.
";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-6";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:61:"Day 7: Kyanjin Gompa to Yala peak Base camp(4800m/15748ft/5h)";s:11:"description";s:363:"We leave the final human settlement in the highland and head towards the rocky glacier route with a fantastic view of the pristine glacier and Himalaya peaks, we walk towards the Yala base camp. upon arrival our team set up camp in appropriate spot, and we start preparing some warm food. Then time for basic climbing skills training for peak. Overnight in tent. ";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-7";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:67:"Day 8: Summit Yala peak (5732m/18802ft) &amp; back to Kyanjin Gompa";s:11:"description";s:614:"The most waiting & exciting day of your trip (Are you ready) today. We leave our camp early in the morning & climb to yala peak. We plan to summit before noon if everything fine. The final 40 meters will be more challenging please listen your body and guide carefully. Once we get top the views are just wow wow such as Shishapangma, Nayak ang, Dorje Lakpa, Langtang Lirung, Ganchenop and many more. Then we slowly desecent to the base camp. About 2 hours we reach back base camp we collecting bag take a rest for while we continue walk back to Kyanjin Gompa for the night. Now it is time to celebrate the victory.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-8";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:53:"Day 9: Kyanjin Gompa to Lama hotel(2380m/7808ft/6-7h)";s:11:"description";s:229:"After breakfast you will trek back from Kyanjin Gompa to lama hotel, retracing your steps and taking in the familiar sights of the region and enjoy the peacefull surroundings the sense of accomplishment as you make your way back.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:6:"item-9";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:58:"Day 10: Trek back from lama to Syabrubesi(1503m/4931ft/5h)";s:11:"description";s:198:"We continue our hike back to Syabrubesi via rimche bamboo a small Sherpa or tamang camp.by lunch time we reach town and enjoy the rest time with the crew. evening enjoy your dinner with strong team.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-10";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:41:"Day 11: Drive back to Kathmandu(1350m/6h)";s:11:"description";s:231:"Today we will drive back to Kathmandu, bringing an end to your Langtang and Yala peak trek. You will reflect on the incredible experience, beautiful landscapes and the sense of accomplishment you have gained throughout the journey.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}s:7:"item-11";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:21:"Day 12: Fly back home";s:11:"description";s:132:"Today you enjoy your last moment in Kathmandu. We will drop you airport for your final departure 3 hours before your flight namaste.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:0:"";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:0:"";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:0:"";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:0:"";}}

a:19:{s:6:"item-0";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:48:"Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)";s:11:"description";s:578:"Welcome to Nepal! Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, our representative will warmly welcome you and transfer you to your hotel in Kathmandu. After check-in, you can relax or explore the vibrant streets of Thamel, famous for its trekking shops, restaurants, and cultural atmosphere.

In the evening, you will meet your trekking and climbing guide for a detailed briefing about the Everest Base Camp with Island Peak Climbing adventure. Equipment will be checked, permits verified, and final preparations completed to ensure you are fully ready for the expedition.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:31:"Tribhuvan International Airport";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:31:"Tribhuvan International Airport";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:17:"Approx. 5–10 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:21:"30–40 minutes drive";s:14:"important_note";s:52:"Arrival and preparation day. Overnight in Kathmandu.";}s:6:"item-1";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:84:"Day 2: Fly to Lukla (2,840 m / 9,317 ft) &amp; Trek to Phakding (2,610 m / 8,562 ft)";s:11:"description";s:443:"An early morning scenic flight takes you to Lukla, offering breathtaking aerial views of the Himalayan range. After meeting the porters and organizing trekking gear, the journey begins with a gentle descent through beautiful Sherpa villages, prayer wheels, suspension bridges, and pine forests.

Following the Dudh Koshi River, you reach the peaceful village of Phakding, where you can relax and enjoy your first night in the Everest region.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:16:"Kathmandu(1350M)";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:17:"Phakding (2,610m)";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:12:"Approx. 8 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:39:"30-minute flight &amp; 3–4 hours trek";s:14:"important_note";s:63:"Flights to Lukla are weather-dependent. Keep your day flexible.";}s:6:"item-2";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:64:"Day 3: Trek from Phakding to Namche Bazaar (3,440 m / 11,286 ft)";s:11:"description";s:320:"Walk through pine forests and cross high suspension bridges spanning the Dudh Koshi River, including the famous Hillary Suspension Bridge. Enter Sagarmatha National Park at Monjo. Take on a steady, steep uphill climb that rewards you with your first views of Mt. Everest before reaching the vibrant hub of Namche Bazaar.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:8:"Phakding";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:13:"Namche Bazaar";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"11 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"5–6 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:69:"Steady ascent gain; stay hydrated and maintain a slow, constant pace.";}s:6:"item-3";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:65:"Day 4: Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar (3,440 m / 11,286 ft)";s:11:"description";s:302:"Essential rest day to adapt to the higher altitude. Take an acclimatization hike up to the Everest View Hotel (3,880 m / 12,729 ft) for panoramic vistas of Mt. Everest, Ama Dablam, Lhotse, and Thamserku. Afterwards, explore the Sherpa Culture Museum or stroll through the local cafes and shops in town.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:13:"Namche Bazaar";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:13:"Namche Bazaar";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:15:"4–5 km (hike)";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:18:"3–4 hours (hike)";s:14:"important_note";s:55:"Hike high, sleep low to help your body adapt smoothly. ";}s:6:"item-4";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:65:"Day 5: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Tengboche (3,860 m / 12,664 ft)";s:11:"description";s:263:"Follow a trail with panoramic views of the Everest range before descending to Phunki Tenga near the river for lunch. The afternoon involves a climb through rhododendron and pine forests up to Tengboche, home to the largest Buddhist monastery in the Khumbu region.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:13:"Namche Bazaar";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:9:"Tengboche";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"10 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"5–6 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:80:"Option to attend the late afternoon prayer ceremony inside Tengboche Monastery. ";}s:6:"item-5";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:61:"Day 6: Trek from Tengboche to Dingboche (4,410 m / 14,468 ft)";s:11:"description";s:273:"Descend through birch and rhododendron forests to Deboche, crossing the Imja River via a suspension bridge. Pass ancient mani walls and ascend gradually past Pangboche village, taking in up-close views of Ama Dablam while continuing into the Imja Valley to reach Dingboche.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:9:"Tengboche";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:9:"Dingboche";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"11 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"5–6 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:49:"You are entering the high-alpine tree-line zone. ";}s:6:"item-6";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:61:"Day 7: Acclimatization Day in Dingboche (4,410 m / 14,468 ft)";s:11:"description";s:226:"econd scheduled acclimatization day. Hike up to Nagarjun Hill (5,100 m / 16,732 ft) or Chhukung Valley for high-altitude training. Enjoy expansive views of Makalu, Lhotse, Chaloche, and the impressive north face of Ama Dablam.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:9:"Dingboche";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:9:"Dingboche";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:11:"5 km (hike)";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:18:"4–5 hours (hike)";s:14:"important_note";s:53:"Rest and recharge for the push toward high elevation.";}s:6:"item-7";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:59:"Day 8: Trek from Dingboche to Lobuche (4,940 m / 16,207 ft)";s:11:"description";s:257:"Trek along the lateral moraine of the Khumbu Glacier. Ascend Thokla Pass (Dughla Pass), home to stone memorials dedicated to climbers who lost their lives in the Everest region. Continue across rough glacial terrain to reach the small settlement of Lobuche.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:9:"Dingboche";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:7:"Lobuche";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"11 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"5–6 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:56:"Dress in layers as temperatures drop significantly here.";}s:6:"item-8";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:111:"Day 9: Trek from Lobuche to Gorakshep (5,170 m / 16,961 ft) &amp; Visit Everest Base Camp (5,364 m / 17,598 ft)";s:11:"description";s:234:"Walk along the rugged moraine of the Khumbu Glacier to Gorakshep. After a brief stop, push onward to Everest Base Camp. Stand beneath the Khumbu Icefall, surrounded by high Himalayan peaks, before returning to Gorakshep for the night.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:7:"Lobuche";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:9:"Gorakshep";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"13 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"7–8 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:128:"High-intensity day over unstable glacial boulders and scree. Headlamps are required in case dusk approaches on the return walk. ";}s:6:"item-9";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:99:"Day 10: Hike to Kala Patthar (5,550 m / 18,208 ft) &amp; Descend to Dingboche (4,410 m / 14,468 ft)";s:11:"description";s:347:"Begin an early pre-dawn climb up Kala Patthar for sunrise views of Mt. Everest, Nuptse, Changtse, and Pumori. Descend to Gorakshep for breakfast, pack up, and retrace your steps back down the valley past Lobuche and Thokla. Continue descending to the lower, oxygen-rich village of Dingboche to rest and recover before starting the Island Peak leg.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:9:"Gorakshep";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:9:"Dingboche";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"15 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"7–8 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:156:"Returning to Dingboche (4,410m) allows your body to recover faster, eat better, and regain full energy before heading up the Imja Valley toward Island Peak.";}s:7:"item-10";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:61:"Day 11: Trek from Dingboche to Chhukung (4,730 m / 15,518 ft)";s:11:"description";s:345:"Take a gentle, easy morning trek gradually ascending east through the Imja Valley. Walk along the riverbed beneath the towering south face of Lhotse and Ama Dablam to reach Chhukung. After arriving, check into the lodge, rest, and organize your technical climbing gear (harness, boots, crampons, ice axe, helmet) with your Sherpa climbing guide.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:9:"Dingboche";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:8:"Chhukung";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:4:"7 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"3–4 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:122:"Short trekking day intended for active rest and finalizing all rental/personal technical gear before moving to Base Camp. ";}s:7:"item-11";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:98:"Day 12: Trek from Chhukung to Island Peak Base Camp (5,200 m / 17,060 ft) &amp; Pre-Climb Training";s:11:"description";s:341:"Trek along the south flank of the Imja Valley, following the moraine trail past Imja Tsho glacier lake to reach Island Peak Base Camp (Pareshaya Gyab). Set up camp in tents. In the afternoon, your climbing Sherpa guide will conduct a mandatory practical session on fixed ropes, jumars/ascenders, crampons, ice axes, and rappelling technique.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:8:"Chhukung";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:21:"Island Peak Base Camp";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:" 6 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:35:"3–4 hours trek + 2 hours training";s:14:"important_note";s:152:"Transition from teahouses to tented camp accommodation. Fresh meals prepared by the camp chef. Early dinner around 5:00 PM; wake-up call is at midnight.";}s:7:"item-12";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:120:"Day 13: Summit Day: Base Camp to Island Peak Summit (6,189 m / 20,305 ft) &amp; Return to Chhukung (4,730 m / 15,518 ft)";s:11:"description";s:466:"Wake up around 12:30 AM for breakfast and begin the summit push by 1:00 AM. Scramble up a rocky gully to High Camp / Crampon Point (5,600m). Put on crampons and rope up to navigate the crevassed glacier. Clip into fixed ropes to climb the steep 40–45° snow headwall up to the narrow summit ridge. Reach the summit of Island Peak (6,189m) for panoramic vistas of Lhotse, Makalu, and Ama Dablam. Abseil down to Base Camp, rest, pack up camp, and return to Chhukung.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:21:"Island Peak Base Camp";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:8:"Chhukung";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"11 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:13:"10–12 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:130:"Coldest, most physically demanding day of the trip. High-level endurance, down outerwear, headlamp, and technical gear mandatory. ";}s:7:"item-13";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:66:"Day 14: Reserve / Contingency Day for Summit (6,189 m / 20,305 ft)";s:11:"description";s:159:"Extra safety buffer day built into the schedule in case bad weather, high ridge winds, or individual acclimatization issues prevent a summit attempt on Day 13.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:8:"Chhukung";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:8:"Chhukung";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:4:"0 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:8:"Flexible";s:14:"important_note";s:152:"If the summit attempt on Day 13 is successful as scheduled, this day serves as a rest day in Chhukung or permits a more relaxed descent down the valley.";}s:7:"item-14";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:73:"Day 15: Trek from Chhukung to Tengboche / Pangboche (3,860 m / 12,664 ft)";s:11:"description";s:276:"Begin the downward trek out of the high alpine valley. Pass Dingboche and descend along the Imja Khola river valley through lower alpine pastures to the village of Pangboche or Tengboche. Noticeably denser oxygen levels and warmer temperatures greet you as you drop elevation.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:8:"Chhukung";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:21:"Tengboche / Pangboche";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"12 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"5–6 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:75:"Easy downhill walking day; enjoy the returning greenery and forested paths.";}s:7:"item-15";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:76:"Day 16: Trek from Tengboche/Pangboche to Namche Bazaar (3,440 m / 11,286 ft)";s:11:"description";s:270:" Descend through rhododendron and pine forests down to Phunki Tenga near the river. Climb up the opposite ridge trail past Kyangjuma and contour around the mountain slopes back into Namche Bazaar. Celebrate your successful summit climb in local bakeries, cafes, or pubs.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:21:"Tengboche / Pangboche";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:13:"Namche Bazaar";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:6:" 10 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"5–6 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:67:"ake advantage of hot showers, bakeries, and Wi-Fi in Namche Bazaar.";}s:7:"item-16";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:61:"Day 17: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Lukla (2,840 m / 9,317 ft)";s:11:"description";s:266:" Final day on the trekking trail. Descend steeply down Namche hill, cross the Hillary Suspension Bridge, and exit Sagarmatha National Park at Monjo. Continue along the Dudh Koshi River through Phakding and Ghat, finishing with a final gentle uphill climb into Lukla.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:13:"Namche Bazaar";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:5:"Lukla";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:5:"19 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:11:"6–7 hours";s:14:"important_note";s:155:"Final evening with your Sherpa guides and porter team; tipping ceremony and celebratory group dinner held in the evening. Overnight at a teahouse in Lukla.";}s:7:"item-17";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:56:"Day 18: Fly from Lukla to Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)";s:11:"description";s:313:"Board an early morning flight from Lukla back to Kathmandu (or Ramechhap/Manthali with drive to Kathmandu). Transfer to your hotel upon arrival. Spend the rest of the afternoon relaxing, shopping for souvenirs in Thamel, or getting a massage. Enjoy a farewell celebration dinner hosted by the team in the evening.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:5:"Lukla";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:15:"Kathmandu Hotel";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:32:"35-minute flight + city transfer";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:0:"";s:14:"important_note";s:145:"Flights out of Lukla depend heavily on mountain weather; having buffer time on Day 18/19 is standard practice. Overnight at a hotel in Kathmandu.";}s:7:"item-18";a:8:{s:12:"heading-trek";s:59:"Day 19: Final Departure from Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)";s:11:"description";s:204:"Enjoy breakfast at your hotel. Depending on your flight schedule, an airport representative will pick you up from your hotel and transfer you to Tribhuvan International Airport for your final flight home.";s:23:"day_wise_gallery_images";s:0:"";s:24:"days_wise_starting_point";s:15:"Kathmandu Hotel";s:21:"day_wise_ending_point";s:31:"Tribhuvan International Airport";s:17:"day_wise_distance";s:9:"5–10 km";s:12:"daywise_hour";s:21:"30–40 minutes drive";s:14:"important_note";s:106:"Airport transfer arranged 3 hours prior to your international flight departure time. Expedition concludes.";}}
